<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef uneven on very light demand and light offerings. Select and Choice rib, round and loin cuts steady to firm, while chuck cuts generally weak. Beef trimmings firm on moderate demand and very light offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>-----</p>
<p>174 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 48 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>19 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     107.15	106.59	102.32	101.84</p>
<p>Changes	   0.38	  0.30	  0.28	  0.23</p>
<p>Rib	  159.34	159.13	148.62	148.04</p>
<p>Chuck	 75.24	 71.60	 75.52	 73.19</p>
<p>Round	 93.22	 93.22	 91.80	 91.80</p>
<p>Loin	 169.72	172.30	153.29	154.62</p>
<p>Brisket     63.09	 63.09	 63.85	 63.85</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  71.83	 71.73	 72.13	 71.92</p>
<p>Flank	 60.83	 60.83	 61.21	 61.21</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
